  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper’s only gate-based quantum experiment is a QAOA Max-Cut benchmark on a 20-node investor graph, evaluated on cuQuantum, Cirq-GPU, and Cirq-IonQ simulators. Reported results were 23.07%/6930.77 s for cuQuantum, 24.18%/15.67 s for Cirq-GPU, and 50.90%/252.57 s for Cirq-IonQ, versus a brute-force baseline of 0% error and 112.62 s. The remaining reported experiments are classical spectral-compression validation studies, including 100 Erdős–Rényi graphs with 50% compression achieving 0.8937 mean approximation ratio at k=15, and 1000 SBM graphs with mean ARI 0.720 ± 0.004.",
